# Multi-agent workflow (AIProposer)

Use this whenever building a slice. Mirrored in the **"Multi-agent workflow"** section of the
root `CLAUDE.md`. Keep both in sync (enforced by `scripts/check_agent_config_sync.py`).

## Sequence (mandatory)

```
PM (slice brief) → Architect (tech spec) → Builder (code) → Tester (report) → PM (accept)
```

Do not skip steps. **No Builder before the Architect has filled the technical section of the slice
file and checked it against the Wave 1 diagrams** (`docs/architecture-sequences.md`, `docs/ai-touchpoints.md`).

## Artifact locations

| Stage | Output | Path |
|---|---|---|
| PM | Slice brief | `docs/agents/slices/S-XXX-*.md` (from `_TEMPLATE.md`) |
| Architect | Tech spec on the slice + optional ADR | Same slice file + `docs/agents/adrs/ADR-XXX-*.md` |
| Builder | Code + doc updates | `backend/`, `frontend/`; Architect updates the Wave 1 docs if the flow changed |
| Tester | Test plan + report | `docs/agents/test-plans/TP-S-XXX-*.md`, `docs/agents/test-reports/TR-S-XXX-*.md` |
| PM | Accept / rework | `Status` field on the slice file |

## Slice sizing

One slice = one PR-sized vertical change. Align to the phases:

- **Phase 1 — Platform skeleton** (Wave 3): Supabase JWT verify, `/v1/me`, proposals CRUD, PATCH
  allowlist, quota counter, mock adapters. LLM adapter returns mock copy or is unplugged.
- **Phase 2 — AI + money** (Wave 4): real LLM adapter, `POST /v1/proposals` + `regenerate`, cached
  server-side PDF, Razorpay checkout + HMAC webhook.
- **Phase 3 — v1.1**: competitor compare (Pro+), infographics, packs. Not before Phase 2 ships.

`S-000-agent-bootstrap` (this wave) is Phase 0: the workflow itself, no product code.

## Read order per agent

1. `mvp-spec.md` §0 locked decisions + the section(s) for the slice's area (§6 data, §7 API, §9 prompt/pricing, §15 leak, §16 injection).
2. `docs/architecture.md` + `docs/architecture-sequences.md` + `docs/ai-touchpoints.md`.
3. The current slice file and any linked ADR.
4. `docs/roadmap.md` to confirm the slice is v0 and not a deferred item.

## Conflict resolution

| Dispute | Owner |
|---|---|
| User value, UX, AC wording, what's in scope | Product Manager |
| API shape, schema, layering, where inference runs | Architect |
| Test coverage, release readiness | Tester |
| "Money never originates in the model" | Non-negotiable (spec §9) — not up for debate |
| Implementation style | The builder rules (`.cursor/rules/backend-fastapi.mdc`, `frontend-nextjs.mdc`) |

## Definition of done (full cycle)

- [ ] All acceptance criteria numbered and testable
- [ ] Architect checklist complete on the slice file; no contradiction with the Wave 1 docs
- [ ] Code on a **feature branch** + PR — never commit on `main` (`.githooks/pre-commit` enforces locally)
- [ ] Every AC mapped to a test (A or M) in the test report
- [ ] If the slice touched an LLM / quota / money / DTO path, `docs/ai-touchpoints.md` still accurate
- [ ] If the slice added or changed a v0 journey, `docs/architecture-sequences.md` updated
- [ ] New deferred ideas recorded in `docs/roadmap.md` (same PR); `mvp-spec.md` untouched
- [ ] `README.md` wave/slice status table updated
- [ ] Parity check passes (`scripts/check_agent_config_sync.py`)
- [ ] PM set `Status: Accepted` on the slice file

## Invoking roles

Tell the agent explicitly: *"Act as Product Manager for slice S-00X"*, *"Act as Architect, fill the
tech spec for S-00X"*, *"Run the full cycle for S-00X"*.

## Claude Code parity

In Claude Code this sequence lives in the "Multi-agent workflow" section of the root `CLAUDE.md`,
and the three roles are subagents in `.claude/agents/` (`product-manager.md`, `architect.md`,
`tester.md`) — invoked the same way, or via the Agent tool with `subagent_type: architect`.
Keep this file and those in sync.
